WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:05.480
Hello, and welcome to your second drink of Stress Relief, part one.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.500
This episode has the famous fire drill cold open.

3
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:15.220
We got so many wonderful tidbits from our crew on how that all went down.

4
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.140
And you know what?

5
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.340
I'm really proud of how we broke down this episode.

6
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:24.440
Lady, it's one of my favorite podcast moments that we did because we really dug into it.

7
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.620
We got so much good stuff.

8
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:30.180
We got a message from Irina S.

9
00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.300
in Russia, who wrote us about the fire drill scene.

10
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:39.100
Irina said, this is one of my favorite episodes ever, naturally, because of the funniest ever

11
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:39.780
cold open.

12
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.000
When I watched it the first time, I couldn't stop laughing.

13
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.640
I think I even teared up.

14
00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.340
That's how funny I found it.

15
00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.860
Now, here is the amazing thing.

16
00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:54.280
Irina went on to say, I work as an English tutor, and whenever I feel like my students

17
00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:59.380
need cheering up or we need to lighten the mood, I ask them, have you seen The Office?

18
00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.940
And most of them say they haven't.

19
00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.260
And so I say, I'm going to show you a little clip.

20
00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:06.100
Just watch.

21
00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:11.020
And I turn on this cold open, and they just lose it.

22
00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.740
It's my favorite thing ever.

23
00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:18.140
I see how they light up watching something with authentic language, and it's just hilarious.

24
00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:23.680
I keep count of how many people began watching the show after my lessons, and so far, it's

25
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:24.480
about five.

26
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:30.520
So my point is, besides being one of the most iconic series ever, your show opens the window

27
00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:35.660
into the American culture and fantastic English language for many students who are learning

28
00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:35.880
it.

29
00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:37.800
Thank you so much.

30
00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:39.880
Oh, that is so fun.

31
00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:44.940
It's very funny to me thinking that this cold open is like an introduction to American

32
00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:45.580
culture.

33
00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:46.440
Oh, no.

34
00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.940
Actually, any clip of The Office.

35
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:50.960
Exactly.

36
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:58.500
Well, this episode also has the super cringe CPR training session, which we've also heard

37
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.080
is used as a teaching tool.

38
00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:00.920
Mike R.

39
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.020
from Portland, Oregon said, it was my birthday, and a small group of friends got

40
00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.220
together to celebrate at a local restaurant.

41
00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:13.000
Everyone had recently experienced some setback or bad luck, myself included.

42
00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.840
One guest had just lost her job.

43
00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:19.500
Another guest found out her first round of IVF treatment didn't take.

44
00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.160
A couple of people shared that one of their kids was having some serious issues, and I

45
00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.440
was having my own medical issue at the time.

46
00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:33.700
As we sat sulking at my sad birthday, a man at another table, unrelated to our group, was

47
00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:34.920
showing signs of choking.

48
00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:38.300
Luckily for him, one of my friends is a doctor.

49
00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:42.060
My friend sprang into action and performed the Heimlich maneuver.

50
00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:48.240
After what seemed like an eternity, a piece of steak was dislodged from the man's throat.

51
00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:53.240
My friend was exhausted mentally and physically after his heroic deed.

52
00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.280
The incident was scary, and I felt helpless.

53
00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:01.480
Realizing that no one else was trained to help that man, I organized a CPR day at my office

54
00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.820
where many office references were made.

55
00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:09.560
Our trainer commented that the office is referenced in nearly every workshop she facilitates.

56
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:15.480
Score one for the guy who lived, and score one for the office for making the world a safer place.

57
00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:23.260
Well, in our breakdown, lady, we talked a lot about how people who have seen this episode

58
00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:31.480
have gone on to, like, save lives because of the stayin' alive tip that the instructor gives.

59
00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:32.480
Yeah, the song.

60
00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.500
Ah, ah, ah, ah, stayin' alive.

61
00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.800
Stayin' alive, stayin' alive.

62
00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:37.480
Exactly.

63
00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:46.140
And speaking of the CPR instructor, we got a letter from Robin Lynch, who plays Rose.

64
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:51.400
In our breakdown, we said, hey, Robin, we're trying to get a hold of you.

65
00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:53.000
Hit us up.

66
00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:53.660
And she did.

67
00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.260
Here's what her letter said.

68
00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.700
Hi, I just listened to your podcast about stress relief.

69
00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.500
Thank you so much for your kind words.

70
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:04.060
I'd love to answer any questions and talk about our day on set.

71
00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.960
It was such an amazing experience.

72
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:15.120
And, lady, I was digging around, and there are, like, four minutes of extra footage from those CPR scenes in the superfan episodes.

73
00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:16.940
So it got us thinking.

74
00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:18.680
Actually, Ange, it got you thinking.

75
00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:28.380
Yeah, I said we should do an Office Lady 6.0 where we talk with Robin, and we can unpack some of the extra scenes and just hear all about her time on set.

76
00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.080
I said I love it.

77
00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.520
So that's what we're going to do.

78
00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:36.300
We've reached out to Robin, and we can't wait to share more in an upcoming Office Lady 6.0.

79
00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:40.280
And now, here's your second drink of stress relief, part one.

80
00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:45.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.

81
00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:47.090
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

82
00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:48.350
We were on The Office together.

83
00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:49.610
And we're best friends.

84
00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:53.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.

85
00:04:53.590 --> 00:05:00.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

86
00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:01.590
