00:27:39.670 --> 00:27:41.370
We have more fan questions.

630
00:27:41.510 --> 00:27:42.670
Angela, Jaden C.

631
00:27:42.830 --> 00:27:47.430
wants to know how many times did Michael throw the projector into the window?

632
00:27:47.790 --> 00:27:49.850
Well, he starts with the chair, right?

633
00:27:50.350 --> 00:27:51.270
That's right.

634
00:27:51.270 --> 00:27:52.850
It does not break.

635
00:27:53.190 --> 00:27:58.050
And Randy said that for that, we used a plane of plexiglass.

636
00:27:58.290 --> 00:27:59.570
Because they didn't want it to break.

637
00:27:59.730 --> 00:28:01.710
They wanted his first attempt not to go well.

638
00:28:01.910 --> 00:28:02.370
Yes.

639
00:28:03.070 --> 00:28:10.110
Then they replaced the plexiglass with breakaway glass, and it shatters very realistically,

640
00:28:10.450 --> 00:28:13.350
but it never shatters in a sharp or dangerous way.

641
00:28:13.890 --> 00:28:15.430
I have a little fun fact for you.

642
00:28:15.730 --> 00:28:20.950
In the olden days of Hollywood, this was known as candy glass.

643
00:28:21.270 --> 00:28:26.510
I know that, Jenna, because I got a tour of an old Western set with my dad, and they

644
00:28:26.510 --> 00:28:31.510
were like, all those windows that guys get thrown out the bars in and the saloon, that

645
00:28:31.510 --> 00:28:32.350
was candy.

646
00:28:32.750 --> 00:28:33.190
Candy.

647
00:28:33.550 --> 00:28:33.690
Yeah.

648
00:28:33.690 --> 00:28:34.510
You could eat it.

649
00:28:34.510 --> 00:28:40.650
I guess nowadays, they don't make it out of candy, but Randy said old schoolers still call it candy glass,

650
00:28:40.790 --> 00:28:43.030
even though now it's called breakaway glass.

651
00:28:43.250 --> 00:28:43.410
Okay.

652
00:28:43.870 --> 00:28:48.690
And Randy also told us, Jaden, in answer to your question, they got it in one take.

653
00:28:49.110 --> 00:28:52.370
One throw of the projector broke the breakaway glass.

654
00:28:52.590 --> 00:28:53.370
There you go.

655
00:28:53.370 --> 00:28:59.070
So, Jaden would also like to know how many times did Kevin break the vending machine?

656
00:28:59.330 --> 00:29:01.370
I reached out to Brian Baumgartner.

