00:44:56.060 --> 00:44:57.600
I was on the edge of my seat.

1023
00:44:57.600 --> 00:44:58.720
I absolutely loved that.

1024
00:44:59.480 --> 00:45:04.340
You guys, the crazy thing is it took me that long to tell that story, but it happened in five seconds.

1025
00:45:04.340 --> 00:45:04.960
Oh my God.

1026
00:45:04.980 --> 00:45:07.500
When we actually filmed it, it was so quick.

1027
00:45:07.880 --> 00:45:12.880
So it was like me, drawer, cat, swing, step out, step mom, Fakie Cat.

1028
00:45:13.140 --> 00:45:14.940
Oh my God, two cats, react to one.

1029
00:45:18.180 --> 00:45:24.580
Well, you mentioned that there was something else going on during all this, which was Oscar going in and out of the ceiling.

1030
00:45:24.860 --> 00:45:27.320
Yes, that was a whole other ordeal.

1031
00:45:27.920 --> 00:45:41.620
Randy told us that that part of the stunt of getting Oscar up into the ceiling was the other most challenging part of the stunt because there was nothing to climb into in the way that our set was built.

1032
00:45:41.620 --> 00:45:48.220
Like the actual lightweight drop ceiling, it was suspended from cables.

1033
00:45:48.660 --> 00:45:51.080
Yeah, very thin rigging wires.

1034
00:45:51.220 --> 00:45:57.340
It was Fakie ceiling, guys, because our set was inside a humongous soundstage.

1035
00:45:57.560 --> 00:45:57.780
Yeah.

1036
00:45:58.040 --> 00:46:01.420
So actually above the Dunder Mifflin offices was just air.

1037
00:46:01.640 --> 00:46:06.760
If you walked outside, you could look up and just see these wires holding Fakie ceiling.

1038
00:46:07.060 --> 00:46:07.280
Yeah.

1039
00:46:07.280 --> 00:46:19.840
So he said in the weeks prior to filming this, our production designer, Michael Gallenberg, and construction coordinator, Tim James, had to completely re-engineer the ceiling.

1040
00:46:20.240 --> 00:46:23.660
They had to like build rafters basically that we didn't have, right?

1041
00:46:23.920 --> 00:46:24.260
Yeah.

1042
00:46:24.460 --> 00:46:29.940
And it had to be enough to support not just Oscar, but all of the stunt personnel.

1043
00:46:29.940 --> 00:46:42.820
He said on the day there were two stunt coordinators, the animal people, Oscar, Oscar stunt double, and an NBC universal safety coordinator all up in the ceiling.

1044
00:46:43.100 --> 00:46:45.180
Can you imagine that guy's day at work?

1045
00:46:45.340 --> 00:46:46.100
I can't.

1046
00:46:46.220 --> 00:46:47.880
Like he's not normally with us.

1047
00:46:48.040 --> 00:46:50.040
He's just up in our ceiling now.

1048
00:46:50.260 --> 00:46:54.920
I can tell you that I had to look up into the ceiling and it looked crowded.

1049
00:46:55.180 --> 00:46:58.280
I get why someone might have missed a cat as it flew up there.

1050
00:47:00.140 --> 00:47:02.880
Well, we got a fan question from Alex M.

1051
00:47:03.220 --> 00:47:05.940
Did Oscar really fall through the ceiling?

1052
00:47:06.900 --> 00:47:07.320
Yes.

1053
00:47:07.580 --> 00:47:08.880
Well, yes and no, right?

1054
00:47:09.100 --> 00:47:12.780
We pulled it off using both Oscar and a stunt double, right, Ange?

1055
00:47:12.860 --> 00:47:13.060
Yeah.

1056
00:47:13.380 --> 00:47:18.200
So I reached out to Oscar and I was like, Oscar, you got to tell us everything about the ceiling.

1057
00:47:18.380 --> 00:47:19.880
I guess he gets asked this a lot.

1058
00:47:20.360 --> 00:47:22.100
And he sent in this audio clip.

1059
00:47:22.460 --> 00:47:23.680
I had a stuntman.

1060
00:47:23.880 --> 00:47:25.400
I had a Moroccan.

1061
00:47:25.400 --> 00:47:28.780
He was, he was, I think he was from Morocco.

1062
00:47:28.800 --> 00:47:32.860
He was, he was, he was from Cirque du Soleil.

1063
00:47:33.180 --> 00:47:36.240
He was a little shorter than me and he was a stuntman.

1064
00:47:36.420 --> 00:47:42.980
And I think he was jumping out from the hole and doing wonderful tumbles when he hit the ground.

1065
00:47:43.400 --> 00:47:44.760
I did half of it.

1066
00:47:44.880 --> 00:47:46.200
He did the really hard part.

1067
00:47:46.460 --> 00:47:48.720
It was a very funny scene, very complicated.

1068
00:47:49.300 --> 00:47:58.240
I remember in one of the shots, I made Steve laugh because one of the ways that I was coming down from the roof on one of them, they had a big,

1069
00:47:58.260 --> 00:48:01.340
a bar up there and it lowered me slowly through the hole.

1070
00:48:01.920 --> 00:48:03.520
And that was a funny way to come down.

1071
00:48:03.640 --> 00:48:07.440
And when I made eye contact with Steve, just hanging there with a straight face, of course, he laughed.

1072
00:48:07.840 --> 00:48:11.180
And then they figured out another way to bring me down, which was the leap down.

1073
00:48:11.320 --> 00:48:18.860
But first I would just like, one of the things we tried was just like being lowered down from the thing, which didn't make sense, but was very funny.

1074
00:48:19.020 --> 00:48:20.180
Do you remember that?

1075
00:48:20.300 --> 00:48:20.980
I remember it.

1076
00:48:21.020 --> 00:48:21.540
I do too.

1077
00:48:21.800 --> 00:48:24.160
It was very weirdly Matrix-y.

1078
00:48:24.380 --> 00:48:24.920
It was.

1079
00:48:24.920 --> 00:48:27.360
And Oscar was slowly coming.

1080
00:48:27.360 --> 00:48:28.320
Like very slowly.

1081
00:48:28.640 --> 00:48:32.260
What was that Tom Cruise movie where he slowly lowered himself down?

1082
00:48:32.360 --> 00:48:33.020
Mission Impossible.

1083
00:48:33.680 --> 00:48:34.520
It was like that.

1084
00:48:34.880 --> 00:48:37.580
Oscar was like slowly coming out of the ceiling.

1085
00:48:37.760 --> 00:48:39.240
It looked crazy.

1086
00:48:39.540 --> 00:48:42.880
And Oscar, of course, did not break because he never broke.

1087
00:48:43.120 --> 00:48:43.760
But we did.

1088
00:48:43.780 --> 00:48:48.280
And all the rest of us were like, we can't possibly continue this if that's physically possible.

1089
00:48:48.520 --> 00:48:51.060
And if Steve broke, you know it looked ridiculous.

1090
00:48:51.060 --> 00:48:55.260
Well, let me break it down for you for anyone who wants to follow along.

1091
00:48:55.440 --> 00:49:01.660
At 2 minutes 38 seconds, the real Oscar is standing on his desk and he pushes up the ceiling tile.

1092
00:49:02.520 --> 00:49:10.640
At 2 minutes 43 seconds, for that beat of Oscar actually jumping up and pulling himself into the ceiling, that's his stunt double.

1093
00:49:10.840 --> 00:49:12.720
You'll notice you don't see his face.

1094
00:49:12.720 --> 00:49:15.260
His double's name was Aladeen Namu.

1095
00:49:15.440 --> 00:49:22.080
And to pull this off, I guess Aladeen had to wear a safety harness underneath his Oscar wardrobe.

1096
00:49:22.520 --> 00:49:30.400
And it had this cable that went up through his harness to a pulley that was manned by two guys in the ceiling.

1097
00:49:30.920 --> 00:49:35.220
And after he would jump, these guys would like hoist him up using this pulley.

1098
00:49:35.440 --> 00:49:37.700
You got to trust the guys in the ceiling, don't you?

1099
00:49:38.420 --> 00:49:42.760
Then at 2 minutes 48 seconds, we see the real Oscar again.

1100
00:49:42.920 --> 00:49:45.320
He's up there in the scaffold looking down.

1101
00:49:45.540 --> 00:49:49.180
He was also secured by a harness and a cable, just to make sure.

1102
00:49:50.180 --> 00:49:59.160
Finally, at 3 minutes 33 seconds, Oscar appears to break through another ceiling panel over by the kitchen near Creed's desk.

1103
00:49:59.520 --> 00:50:01.620
That's his stunt double's legs kicking.

1104
00:50:02.120 --> 00:50:05.700
Creed's reaction was so hilarious to me.

1105
00:50:05.840 --> 00:50:06.500
Sorry, go on.

1106
00:50:06.500 --> 00:50:13.320
But at 4 minutes, 6 seconds, that is when the stunt team dropped real Oscar onto the floor.

1107
00:50:13.620 --> 00:50:15.480
So many beats of this scene.

1108
00:50:15.600 --> 00:50:16.300
So many.

1109
00:50:16.640 --> 00:50:20.260
We haven't even talked about Stanley's heart attack.

1110
00:50:20.440 --> 00:50:21.320
Oh my gosh.

1111
00:50:21.700 --> 00:50:24.120
At the end of all of this, he's on the ground.

1112
00:50:25.300 --> 00:50:28.560
And Michael is like telling him he can't die.

1113
00:50:28.660 --> 00:50:29.160
He can't die.

1114
00:50:29.360 --> 00:50:30.740
He's shoving a wallet in his mouth.

1115
00:50:30.900 --> 00:50:32.960
Yeah, Michael's yelling, Barack Obama's president.

1116
00:50:32.960 --> 00:50:34.580
You can't die, Stanley.

1117
00:50:35.180 --> 00:50:37.440
We got a fan question from Megan G.

1118
00:50:38.200 --> 00:50:45.340
Leslie David Baker spoke at my college and said that the scene where Michael puts the wallet in his mouth was improvised.

1119
00:50:45.700 --> 00:50:46.900
Is this true?

1120
00:50:47.820 --> 00:50:49.840
Lady, I looked it up in the script.

1121
00:50:50.040 --> 00:50:51.080
It is not there.

1122
00:50:51.520 --> 00:50:55.240
It ended with him saying, you can't die, Barack Obama is president.

1123
00:50:55.240 --> 00:50:58.240
That wallet bit was on the day.

1124
00:50:58.480 --> 00:50:59.760
Oh my gosh.

1125
00:51:00.080 --> 00:51:02.860
Well, I have a fan question that made me chuckle, Jenna.

1126
00:51:03.560 --> 00:51:04.240
Emma N.

1127
00:51:04.360 --> 00:51:07.980
wrote in and said, Meredith has these kind of dirty?

1128
00:51:08.180 --> 00:51:08.940
Question mark.

1129
00:51:09.300 --> 00:51:13.000
Brown boots she's carrying at around 1 minute 49 seconds.

1130
00:51:13.420 --> 00:51:18.460
And throughout some of the cold open, was there any deleted scene or explanation about this?

1131
00:51:18.460 --> 00:51:19.000
Oh.

1132
00:51:19.200 --> 00:51:20.760
Well, Emma, you got me curious.

1133
00:51:20.800 --> 00:51:22.540
I went to your time code.

1134
00:51:22.700 --> 00:51:23.760
You are not wrong.

1135
00:51:23.960 --> 00:51:24.820
I took a photo.

1136
00:51:25.000 --> 00:51:26.360
Look, Jenna, I'll put it in stories.

1137
00:51:26.720 --> 00:51:27.840
What is that?

1138
00:51:27.860 --> 00:51:32.680
I was like, Emma, I recognize these boots.

1139
00:51:32.980 --> 00:51:40.620
I would bet money that those are Kate's UGG boots that wardrobe gave us to keep under our desk when we were so cold.

1140
00:51:40.940 --> 00:51:42.860
They're not Meredith's boots.

1141
00:51:42.860 --> 00:51:44.540
So I texted Kate.

1142
00:51:45.500 --> 00:51:53.360
I said, Kate, in stress relief when Dwight almost burns down the building, did you grab your actual UGG boots from under your desk?

1143
00:51:53.600 --> 00:51:54.700
Fans are asking.

1144
00:51:55.360 --> 00:51:59.300
And I sent her the picture and she wrote back, ha, ha, ha, I did.

1145
00:52:00.420 --> 00:52:04.540
So the direction we were given was clearly everyone's panicking and they're grabbing their things.

1146
00:52:04.540 --> 00:52:05.760
They want to get out of the building.

1147
00:52:05.760 --> 00:52:08.100
And she said, I grabbed my UGG boots.

1148
00:52:08.240 --> 00:52:09.720
They are actually not dirty.

1149
00:52:09.840 --> 00:52:11.220
They're a dusty pink.

1150
00:52:11.620 --> 00:52:12.020
Oh.

1151
00:52:12.020 --> 00:52:13.360
So there you go, Emma.

1152
00:52:13.560 --> 00:52:14.260
Nice catch.

1153
00:52:14.820 --> 00:52:17.200
Lady, I think we should take a break.

1154
00:52:17.460 --> 00:52:18.680
That's the cold open.

1155
00:52:18.880 --> 00:52:20.220
That's just the cold open.

1156
00:52:20.360 --> 00:52:24.680
We still have this whole episode to break down and there is so much more to talk about.

1157
00:52:24.960 --> 00:52:25.520
All right.

1158
00:52:25.620 --> 00:52:26.320
We'll be back.

1159
00:52:34.920 --> 00:52:35.460
All right.

1160
00:52:35.540 --> 00:52:36.340
We are back.

1161
00:52:36.640 --> 00:52:43.960
Dwight and Michael are at a meeting in corporate because, um, hi, Dwight almost burned the building down and Stanley had a heart attack.

1162
00:52:44.360 --> 00:52:48.920
So they're having to meet with David Wallace and Kendall from HR.

1163
00:52:49.180 --> 00:52:50.100
Yes, Kendall.

1164
00:52:50.280 --> 00:52:51.520
Guest star alert.

1165
00:52:51.720 --> 00:52:53.540
Kendall was played by John Hartman.

1166
00:52:53.780 --> 00:52:55.380
Now we've heard of Kendall before.

1167
00:52:55.560 --> 00:52:58.940
He was mentioned in previous episodes and we heard his voice.

1168
00:52:58.940 --> 00:53:00.720
Remember when he yelled at Holly?

1169
00:53:01.040 --> 00:53:01.760
Oh, yeah.

1170
00:53:01.760 --> 00:53:04.140
So John Hartman did the voice.

1171
00:53:04.360 --> 00:53:05.580
And now here he is.

1172
00:53:05.700 --> 00:53:06.660
He's at the table.

1173
00:53:06.840 --> 00:53:07.840
He was so good.

1174
00:53:08.100 --> 00:53:12.300
You know that bit where they do the little runner where, like, take heed, heeded?

1175
00:53:12.620 --> 00:53:14.620
Did you look it up to see if it was scripted?

1176
00:53:14.620 --> 00:53:17.780
I did because Sonia Y wanted to know.

1177
00:53:18.140 --> 00:53:19.480
Sonia, so did I.

1178
00:53:19.740 --> 00:53:21.160
It was scripted.

1179
00:53:21.240 --> 00:53:26.420
It was scripted until the very last Michael heeded again.

1180
00:53:26.920 --> 00:53:27.360
Yes.

1181
00:53:27.700 --> 00:53:29.140
They kind of added to the bit.

1182
00:53:29.400 --> 00:53:31.760
Steve added to the bit at the very end.

1183
00:53:31.880 --> 00:53:33.260
But everything else is scripted.

1184
00:53:33.340 --> 00:53:36.860
I actually texted that couplet of dialogue to Paul Lieberstein.

1185
00:53:36.920 --> 00:53:37.900
I said, this is perfection.

1186
00:53:37.900 --> 00:53:38.860
You were so funny.

1187
00:53:39.480 --> 00:53:42.180
And then Steve at the very end added one more.

1188
00:53:42.320 --> 00:53:44.140
And I can see Rain trying not to break.

1189
00:53:44.300 --> 00:53:45.820
He actually has to look down at the table.

1190
00:53:46.320 --> 00:53:46.480
Yeah.

1191
00:53:47.580 --> 00:53:50.600
There's two things I have to point out also in this scene.

1192
00:53:50.900 --> 00:53:55.200
First of all, in this dialogue, Dwight's like, imagine my frustration.

1193
00:53:55.200 --> 00:53:57.640
A safety officer that they're not listening.

1194
00:53:58.340 --> 00:53:59.260
Excuse me?

1195
00:53:59.580 --> 00:54:02.460
Angela Martin was the safety officer in basketball.

1196
00:54:03.220 --> 00:54:06.260
She couldn't find the first aid kit because Dwight had moved it.

1197
00:54:06.340 --> 00:54:08.780
And she said, how many times do I have to tell you?

1198
00:54:08.860 --> 00:54:10.520
I'm the safety officer.

1199
00:54:10.920 --> 00:54:13.660
It was like their first little, like, spat.

1200
00:54:13.880 --> 00:54:14.060
Yeah.

1201
00:54:14.520 --> 00:54:15.660
So I don't know what's happened.

1202
00:54:15.800 --> 00:54:17.600
Dwight clearly has not let this go.

1203
00:54:17.600 --> 00:54:19.440
And he thinks he's the safety officer.

1204
00:54:19.700 --> 00:54:21.520
Well, he's not the safety officer anymore.

1205
00:54:21.780 --> 00:54:22.480
No, he's not.

1206
00:54:22.540 --> 00:54:24.440
Because Michael's going to be the safety man.

1207
00:54:25.000 --> 00:54:26.100
That's what he calls it.

1208
00:54:26.160 --> 00:54:27.400
He calls it the safety man.

1209
00:54:27.600 --> 00:54:32.740
I have one other thing I have to point out because it made me laugh so hard, Jenna.

1210
00:54:32.980 --> 00:54:35.740
I rewound this and watched this beat three times.

1211
00:54:35.740 --> 00:54:40.820
When Michael gets up and walks out and looks out at the city, you know, and then he comes

1212
00:54:40.820 --> 00:54:42.260
and sits down next to Kendall.

1213
00:54:42.520 --> 00:54:46.700
He, like, scooches Kendall over and he says, can you shove it down, please?

1214
00:54:46.960 --> 00:54:48.020
Shove it down, please.

1215
00:54:48.300 --> 00:54:49.260
I didn't catch that.

1216
00:54:49.460 --> 00:54:51.160
It's so funny.

1217
00:54:51.340 --> 00:54:52.600
That is not in the script.

1218
00:54:53.060 --> 00:54:54.280
Shove it down, please.

1219
00:54:54.320 --> 00:54:55.700
It's not in the script.

1220
00:54:56.460 --> 00:55:01.740
And the way that John and Andy Buckley just rolled with all of those little moments.

1221
00:55:01.920 --> 00:55:03.020
Oh, they're so good.

1222
00:55:03.300 --> 00:55:08.920
Well, when they get back to Dunder Mifflin, Stanley is coming back into the office.

1223
00:55:09.260 --> 00:55:11.380
Michael's like, shh, quiet, quiet, quiet.

1224
00:55:11.640 --> 00:55:12.600
No loud noises.

1225
00:55:12.820 --> 00:55:13.000
Yeah.

1226
00:55:13.480 --> 00:55:14.360
No surprises.

1227
00:55:15.040 --> 00:55:15.180
Yeah.

1228
00:55:15.680 --> 00:55:20.940
Stanley has a talking head where he explains that in the past, he has been very abrupt with

1229
00:55:20.940 --> 00:55:26.080
people, but the doctor said he needs to find a more positive way to relate to people or

1230
00:55:26.080 --> 00:55:26.880
he will die.

1231
00:55:27.140 --> 00:55:27.500
Mm-hmm.

1232
00:55:27.820 --> 00:55:30.260
Well, you notice in that talking head, there was a montage.

1233
00:55:30.600 --> 00:55:34.260
A montage of moments of Stanley being abrupt with people.

1234
00:55:34.460 --> 00:55:35.740
Yeah, of him losing his cool.

1235
00:55:35.980 --> 00:55:38.780
A montage like this was very unusual for our show.

1236
00:55:39.280 --> 00:55:45.400
It was added to help give more context to the character of Stanley for all of those post-Super

1237
00:55:45.400 --> 00:55:46.080
Bowl viewers.

1238
00:55:46.400 --> 00:55:49.140
I was going to say, because a documentary doesn't do a montage.

1239
00:55:49.400 --> 00:55:50.100
Not normally.

1240
00:55:50.320 --> 00:55:50.780
Not normally.

1241
00:55:50.980 --> 00:55:52.800
But when you're after the Super Bowl-

1242
00:55:52.800 --> 00:55:53.140
You do.

1243
00:55:53.180 --> 00:55:53.540
You do.

1244
00:55:53.920 --> 00:55:58.340
Another beat of the scene that didn't make it in, it's in the deleted scenes that really

1245
00:55:58.340 --> 00:56:03.200
made me laugh, Jenna, is that Michael, you know, wants everyone to help Stanley.

1246
00:56:03.520 --> 00:56:04.360
He's urging them.

1247
00:56:04.540 --> 00:56:06.840
So here is how that manifests.

