Andy makes Stanley a mix CD of Enya songs.

1249
00:56:11.900 --> 00:56:12.100
Oh.

1250
00:56:13.240 --> 00:56:14.340
Stanley's like, thanks.

1251
00:56:14.340 --> 00:56:17.720
Michael assigns Kevin to be his bathroom buddy.

1252
00:56:18.480 --> 00:56:18.960
Okay.

1253
00:56:19.240 --> 00:56:22.080
As Kevin says, in case you have a heart attack on the crapper.

1254
00:56:22.440 --> 00:56:22.660
Okay.

1255
00:56:22.840 --> 00:56:25.500
And Stanley's like, I can go to the bathroom by myself.

1256
00:56:25.660 --> 00:56:25.960
Thank you.

1257
00:56:26.800 --> 00:56:28.740
Phyllis just looks at him and can't stop smiling.

1258
00:56:29.240 --> 00:56:34.200
And she has a really sweet talking head where she says she's known Stanley Hudson a long

1259
00:56:34.200 --> 00:56:39.760
time, and the way he breathes, his sort of loud breathing is soothing to her.

1260
00:56:40.420 --> 00:56:41.560
It's really cute.

1261
00:56:42.020 --> 00:56:43.520
So you have that Phyllis moment.

1262
00:56:43.980 --> 00:56:48.100
And then Michael says, don't worry, Stanley, I got you a portable defibrillator.

1263
00:56:48.440 --> 00:56:48.780
Oh.

1264
00:56:49.420 --> 00:56:51.260
And then tries to go put it on him.

1265
00:56:51.320 --> 00:56:52.600
And everyone's like, no, no, no, no, no, no.

1266
00:56:52.720 --> 00:56:53.280
Oh, my gosh.

1267
00:56:53.300 --> 00:56:54.380
I remember shooting that.

1268
00:56:54.560 --> 00:56:54.760
Yes.

1269
00:56:54.880 --> 00:56:58.680
And then Michael, like, thinks it's funny and wants to, like, hook everyone up to it.

1270
00:56:58.680 --> 00:57:00.560
Wants to defibrillate.

1271
00:57:00.560 --> 00:57:01.020
Yes.

1272
00:57:01.300 --> 00:57:01.660
How do you say that?

1273
00:57:02.020 --> 00:57:02.860
Defibrillate people.

1274
00:57:02.960 --> 00:57:03.010
Everybody.

1275
00:57:03.460 --> 00:57:07.780
And then Kevin gets the defibrillator and, as a joke, puts it on Meredith's seat.

1276
00:57:08.120 --> 00:57:12.600
Meredith sits on it and doesn't even notice it, but all of her hair goes up in the air.

1277
00:57:12.720 --> 00:57:14.420
And that's another stunt we had to do.

1278
00:57:14.580 --> 00:57:17.520
They had to make Kate Flannery's hair rise up with static.

1279
00:57:18.180 --> 00:57:18.400
Wow.

1280
00:57:18.820 --> 00:57:20.540
Didn't make it in, but it was pretty funny.

1281
00:57:21.040 --> 00:57:26.620
Michael is determined to make sure that we all know what to do should Stanley ever have

1282
00:57:26.620 --> 00:57:27.760
another heart attack.

1283
00:57:30.560 --> 00:57:32.100
room for a CPR class.

1284
00:57:32.260 --> 00:57:32.760
Yes.

1285
00:57:33.000 --> 00:57:41.980
A class he wishes he was running, but apparently you have to have an actual CPR trainer or else

1286
00:57:41.980 --> 00:57:42.880
you don't get the dummy.

1287
00:57:43.300 --> 00:57:43.740
Yeah.

1288
00:57:43.900 --> 00:57:49.720
The Red Cross won't give you the dummy doll unless you have an actually trained CPR instructor.

1289
00:57:50.000 --> 00:57:51.460
We got a fan question.

1290
00:57:51.560 --> 00:57:51.780
Okay.

1291
00:57:52.080 --> 00:57:53.120
From Stephanie H.

1292
00:57:53.600 --> 00:57:54.980
I loved this question.

1293
00:57:55.400 --> 00:57:59.280
Who played Rose, the CPR instructor, and why is she so perfect?

1294
00:57:59.280 --> 00:58:03.000
She is absolutely amazing.

1295
00:58:03.320 --> 00:58:05.480
Her name is Robin Lynch.

1296
00:58:05.700 --> 00:58:07.220
She is an actress.

1297
00:58:07.660 --> 00:58:10.540
I believed she was a CPR trainer.

1298
00:58:10.980 --> 00:58:18.640
I reached out to Allison Jones, and she said she found Robin through just a general casting

1299
00:58:18.640 --> 00:58:23.900
call and that Robin was by far the best person that they saw for the role.

1300
00:58:23.900 --> 00:58:26.920
She just plays it so perfectly straight.

1301
00:58:27.120 --> 00:58:28.560
She's there to teach CPR.

1302
00:58:28.940 --> 00:58:33.180
This office goes off the rails, and she just tries to stay the course.

1303
00:58:33.380 --> 00:58:36.160
I did slide into her DMs on Insta.

1304
00:58:36.260 --> 00:58:38.380
Yeah, Robin, we tried to get a hold of you.

1305
00:58:38.580 --> 00:58:39.860
We wanted to chat with you, Robin.

1306
00:58:39.860 --> 00:58:42.080
If you ever see our message, let us know.

1307
00:58:42.260 --> 00:58:43.560
We'll chat you up in a revisited.

1308
00:58:44.060 --> 00:58:47.880
Should we talk about all the things that go wrong in this CPR class?

1309
00:58:47.940 --> 00:58:48.560
There are many.

1310
00:58:48.560 --> 00:58:49.260
There are many.

1311
00:58:49.400 --> 00:58:51.080
First of all, it starts with Kevin.

1312
00:58:51.420 --> 00:58:53.200
Kevin gives out at 20 seconds.

1313
00:58:53.340 --> 00:58:54.320
He's like, I'm calling it.

1314
00:58:54.500 --> 00:58:54.760
Yeah.

1315
00:58:55.160 --> 00:58:57.480
And then Rose is like, does anyone else want to turn?

1316
00:58:57.680 --> 00:59:00.480
And Dwight says absolutely he would not.

1317
00:59:00.740 --> 00:59:08.200
And as the camera is pulling back away from Dwight to reveal the room, Jenna, at 9 minutes,

1318
00:59:08.320 --> 00:59:12.860
50 seconds, I am whispering to someone off camera, no.

1319
00:59:13.260 --> 00:59:14.380
What are you talking about?

1320
00:59:14.460 --> 00:59:14.700
What are you saying?

1321
00:59:14.700 --> 00:59:15.980
I'm not looking at Rose.

1322
00:59:16.060 --> 00:59:17.840
I'm looking at someone off camera.

1323
00:59:17.980 --> 00:59:19.800
I don't know who I'm talking to.

1324
00:59:20.000 --> 00:59:21.720
Wait, let me ask you this question.

1325
00:59:22.180 --> 00:59:22.560
What?

1326
00:59:22.740 --> 00:59:26.240
Could you be saying no to the other camera?

1327
00:59:26.720 --> 00:59:28.460
I think so, maybe.

1328
00:59:28.460 --> 00:59:32.680
But it looks really weird, and I filmed it, and I'm going to show it to you.

1329
00:59:32.820 --> 00:59:35.860
And I'll put this in stories, but first I'm going to show my BFF guys.

1330
00:59:36.440 --> 00:59:36.880
Okay, ready?

1331
00:59:37.140 --> 00:59:37.720
Hit play.

1332
00:59:38.160 --> 00:59:50.800
I'm finally saying no.

1333
00:59:51.500 --> 00:59:53.160
And look, look at my face.

1334
00:59:53.940 --> 00:59:54.380
No.

1335
00:59:54.380 --> 00:59:58.880
I think, I don't know if that's an improv you're doing, if you're doing it to camera.

1336
00:59:59.460 --> 01:00:02.680
I think it's an improv that I'm doing to Matt Sohn, B camera.

1337
01:00:03.060 --> 01:00:03.260
Yeah.

1338
01:00:03.800 --> 01:00:08.160
Angela in Deleted Scenes had a talking head where she's like, I am not putting my mouth

1339
01:00:08.160 --> 01:00:08.900
on that thing.

1340
01:00:09.020 --> 01:00:10.600
Who knows whose mouth has been on it?

1341
01:00:10.760 --> 01:00:14.760
So I think I was sort of improvising off that talking head.

1342
01:00:14.840 --> 01:00:17.460
But it looks really random if you catch it.

1343
01:00:17.560 --> 01:00:19.360
It's a very, very good catch, lady.

1344
01:00:19.360 --> 01:00:24.640
Well, Stanley's going to give it a go, because for some reason, Michael thinks Stanley should

1345
01:00:24.640 --> 01:00:26.680
learn how to resuscitate himself.

1346
01:00:26.940 --> 01:00:28.180
We might not always be there.

1347
01:00:28.480 --> 01:00:28.720
Right.

1348
01:00:29.040 --> 01:00:33.140
And then, of course, in true Michael fashion, he takes over the meeting, right?

1349
01:00:33.180 --> 01:00:35.380
He's going to tell them how to do CPR now.

1350
01:00:35.620 --> 01:00:35.820
Right.

1351
01:00:35.820 --> 01:00:38.180
And they're doing it all wrong.

1352
01:00:38.540 --> 01:00:41.460
Rose says, listen, guys, you need 100 beats per minute.

1353
01:00:41.720 --> 01:00:46.500
And she suggests they pump to the tune of Staying Alive by the Bee Gees.

1354
01:00:46.700 --> 01:00:46.960
Mm-hmm.

1355
01:00:47.300 --> 01:00:50.440
At first, Michael confuses this with I Will Survive.

1356
01:00:50.660 --> 01:00:51.060
Mm-hmm.

1357
01:00:51.060 --> 01:00:59.740
But then, Rose starts singing Staying Alive, you know, uh, uh, uh, uh, staying alive, staying

1358
01:00:59.740 --> 01:01:00.280
alive.

1359
01:01:00.840 --> 01:01:07.540
Then, Andy starts singing Staying Alive, Kelly starts dancing, it turns into a dance party.

1360
01:01:07.800 --> 01:01:10.480
I actually have the clip if you want to hear it.

1361
01:01:10.540 --> 01:01:11.260
Let's hear it.

1362
01:01:12.000 --> 01:01:15.860
Ah, ah, ah, ah, staying alive, staying alive.

1363
01:01:16.080 --> 01:01:20.240
Ah, ah, ah, ah, staying alive, staying alive.

1364
01:01:20.240 --> 01:01:23.440
You can't tell by the way I use my walk.

1365
01:01:23.440 --> 01:01:25.480
I'm a woman's man, no time to talk.

1366
01:01:25.880 --> 01:01:29.640
Words of loud women won't been kicked around since I was born.

1367
01:01:29.880 --> 01:01:31.740
Well, it's all right, it's okay.

1368
01:01:31.980 --> 01:01:33.980
You can look the other way.

1369
01:01:34.240 --> 01:01:38.520
Look at me, look at me, look at me, look at me.

1370
01:01:38.580 --> 01:01:40.840
I'ma, I'ma, I'ma, I'ma, I'ma, I'ma, I'ma, I'ma, I'ma, I'ma, I'ma, I'ma, I'ma,

1371
01:01:40.900 --> 01:01:42.500
Staying Alive, Staying Alive.

1372
01:01:42.620 --> 01:01:44.340
I mean, poor Rose.

1373
01:01:45.560 --> 01:01:48.420
We had a fan question from Megan D.

1374
01:01:48.680 --> 01:01:49.260
in Scotland.

1375
01:01:49.260 --> 01:01:56.580
Was any of the scene with the Red Cross lady improvised, such as Kelly's dancing or Andy's singing?

1376
01:01:57.200 --> 01:01:58.300
No, guys.

1377
01:01:58.580 --> 01:02:01.440
This whole thing, all the singing and the dancing, it was all scripted.

1378
01:02:01.900 --> 01:02:05.240
And we followed this scene pretty much as written.

1379
01:02:05.600 --> 01:02:06.660
Brilliantly written.

1380
01:02:06.980 --> 01:02:10.140
I found out who pitched this idea.

1381
01:02:10.400 --> 01:02:11.260
Oh, I know.

1382
01:02:11.400 --> 01:02:11.840
Tell them.

1383
01:02:12.060 --> 01:02:14.760
It is Jen Salata.

1384
01:02:14.960 --> 01:02:15.500
Yes.

1385
01:02:15.500 --> 01:02:20.080
This whole staying alive CPR idea came from her.

1386
01:02:20.280 --> 01:02:22.680
She said that she had heard it was true.

1387
01:02:22.980 --> 01:02:25.480
She looked it up and cross-checked it.

1388
01:02:25.600 --> 01:02:30.080
She said she cross-checked it again because she didn't want to put it on TV unless it was true.

1389
01:02:30.620 --> 01:02:36.540
And then she shared with me that before the office, she had been a writer's assistant on Home Improvement.

1390
01:02:36.820 --> 01:02:43.860
And that the writers had done an episode where the Jonathan Taylor Thomas character found a lump on his throat.

1391
01:02:43.860 --> 01:02:48.540
And it turned out that it was a thyroid issue in the episode, right?

1392
01:02:48.800 --> 01:02:51.940
And Jen said that she was later in charge of opening the mail.

1393
01:02:52.120 --> 01:02:59.500
And they got letters from all of these families that said after watching that episode, it helped save their children's lives.

1394
01:02:59.960 --> 01:03:02.560
Because their children had had a thyroid lump.

1395
01:03:02.720 --> 01:03:05.160
And because of the episode, they got it checked out.

1396
01:03:05.160 --> 01:03:14.500
And guys, since this stress relief episode aired, people have used this CPR technique to save lives.

1397
01:03:14.780 --> 01:03:15.880
They have.

1398
01:03:16.480 --> 01:03:24.820
Jen shared with us that she heard about a guy pulling a woman out of a car and doing CPR to the tune of staying alive because of this episode.

1399
01:03:25.000 --> 01:03:26.100
I looked it up.

1400
01:03:26.200 --> 01:03:26.880
It's true.

1401
01:03:27.080 --> 01:03:28.000
There's many articles.

1402
01:03:28.180 --> 01:03:29.140
I'm going to start with this one.

1403
01:03:29.140 --> 01:03:34.080
Okay, in January of 2019, Rolling Stones ran this story.

1404
01:03:34.620 --> 01:03:43.340
A scene from the office that dealt with first aid technique is credited to helping save a life after an Arizona man, despite having no CPR training,

1405
01:03:43.860 --> 01:03:46.400
managed to resuscitate a woman in medical distress.

1406
01:03:46.720 --> 01:03:50.260
His name, interestingly enough, is Cross Scott.

1407
01:03:50.480 --> 01:03:51.000
Whoa.

1408
01:03:51.200 --> 01:03:52.420
Yeah, his last name is Scott.

1409
01:03:52.420 --> 01:03:58.720
So, he found an unconscious woman behind the wheel of her car that was rolling down a dirt road.

1410
01:03:58.980 --> 01:03:59.440
Wow.

1411
01:03:59.840 --> 01:04:07.480
He smashed the window, got her out, and then he's quoted as saying, I've never prepared myself for CPR in my life.

1412
01:04:07.480 --> 01:04:09.020
I had no idea what I was doing.

1413
01:04:10.180 --> 01:04:17.440
Thankfully, Scott had seen the episode of the office that dealt with CPR training and knew to do chest compressions to the cadence of staying alive.

1414
01:04:17.440 --> 01:04:27.260
They reached out to Courtney Slaniker, executive director of the Red Cross Southern Arizona chapter, and she told the Daily Star that if you don't do CPR, the victim will die.

1415
01:04:27.480 --> 01:04:28.520
Don't be afraid to act.

1416
01:04:28.660 --> 01:04:32.160
Whatever you do will help that victim and hopefully prevent a death.

1417
01:04:32.300 --> 01:04:39.020
And Courtney confirmed that staying alive is, in fact, the correct rhythm for chest compressions.

1418
01:04:39.660 --> 01:04:39.920
Wow.

1419
01:04:40.160 --> 01:04:42.160
Jen Salata, you got it right.

1420
01:04:42.960 --> 01:04:43.520
Wow.

1421
01:04:43.520 --> 01:04:53.860
There are so many, guys, but just recently, in January of this year, the Today Show shared a story about a four-year-old girl who collapsed while playing tag, and her dad,

1422
01:04:54.020 --> 01:05:00.440
Matt Uber, found her and started chest compressions, again, to the tune of staying alive.

1423
01:05:00.620 --> 01:05:04.900
And he's quoted as saying, when I was trying to think about what to do about CPR,

1424
01:05:05.340 --> 01:05:12.440
my mind literally went to that episode of the office where they are doing CPR training and doing the compressions to the beat of staying alive.

1425
01:05:12.440 --> 01:05:16.740
I mean, that just got me choked up to imagine that father in that moment.

1426
01:05:16.740 --> 01:05:17.420
I know.

1427
01:05:17.420 --> 01:05:20.140
And then he had something, anything he could do.

1428
01:05:20.340 --> 01:05:21.140
I know.

1429
01:05:22.080 --> 01:05:22.820
I know.

1430
01:05:22.900 --> 01:05:23.500
And there's more.

1431
01:05:23.700 --> 01:05:27.120
I know there's more stories, but those two were two that stood out to me.

1432
01:05:27.720 --> 01:05:28.080
Amazing.

1433
01:05:28.380 --> 01:05:38.380
And one of the things that, after reading some of these stories, Jenna, that people share is that how important knowing CPR is and that we should all learn CPR.

1434
01:05:38.380 --> 01:05:45.760
Yes, we have the staying alive, so you know the beats, but that we should all learn our CPR safety because it really can save a life.

1435
01:05:45.920 --> 01:05:54.280
I know that when we had our son, our first child, Lee and I both did an infant CPR training.

1436
01:05:54.280 --> 01:05:54.880
Same, same.

1437
01:05:55.060 --> 01:05:56.360
But we should do a refresher.

1438
01:05:56.600 --> 01:05:56.860
Yeah.

1439
01:05:57.100 --> 01:05:58.780
Well, it's not over for Rose.

1440
01:05:59.000 --> 01:06:00.320
She's not out of the woods yet.

1441
01:06:00.500 --> 01:06:01.880
Things are about to get even crazier.

1442
01:06:01.880 --> 01:06:09.000
Yeah, she announces that we failed to save the life of our CPR dummy.

1443
01:06:09.880 --> 01:06:16.840
Dwight suggests that the next course of action would be to harvest the organs for organ donation.

1444
01:06:17.140 --> 01:06:21.300
And then he, of course, grabs the giant knife that is strapped to his calf.

1445
01:06:21.760 --> 01:06:22.020
Yeah.

1446
01:06:22.220 --> 01:06:25.060
And he hacks into the dummy's cheSt.

1447
01:06:25.320 --> 01:06:25.500
Yeah.

1448
01:06:25.620 --> 01:06:26.980
And we all freak out.

1449
01:06:26.980 --> 01:06:30.280
Yeah, we freak out because then he cuts off the dummy's face.

1450
01:06:30.460 --> 01:06:32.320
And puts it on his face.

1451
01:06:32.500 --> 01:06:33.700
Like Silence of the Lambs.

1452
01:06:33.800 --> 01:06:34.000
Yeah.

1453
01:06:34.460 --> 01:06:36.100
We had some fan mail about it.

1454
01:06:36.360 --> 01:06:40.640
People would like to know how many CPR dummies were used in this episode.

1455
01:06:41.120 --> 01:06:41.440
Hmm.

1456
01:06:42.080 --> 01:06:43.640
Well, I asked Randy.

1457
01:06:43.920 --> 01:06:45.020
I know for sure.

1458
01:06:45.180 --> 01:06:48.340
Rain really did cut into it because we watched him do it.

1459
01:06:48.620 --> 01:06:52.580
Randy said we used three CPR mannequins in total.

1460
01:06:52.580 --> 01:06:58.740
Now, in a minute, David Wallace is going to say that they cost $3,500 each.

1461
01:06:58.980 --> 01:07:01.100
But Randy said that was a little exaggerated.

1462
01:07:01.460 --> 01:07:07.320
He said there are some top-end dummies that come with very sophisticated features like articulating

1463
01:07:07.320 --> 01:07:09.040
heads and heartbeat simulators.

1464
01:07:09.540 --> 01:07:12.900
Those cost, at the time, around $1,000 each.

1465
01:07:13.040 --> 01:07:17.900
But we used one that cost about $750 each.

1466
01:07:18.300 --> 01:07:18.940
Okay.

1467
01:07:19.420 --> 01:07:22.220
But listen, Dwight is in trouble again.

1468
01:07:22.580 --> 01:07:28.320
He has to go back to corporate and he has to discuss his mutilation of the CPR dummy.

1469
01:07:28.520 --> 01:07:32.340
I really can't believe the guy is still employed.

1470
01:07:32.760 --> 01:07:33.720
I know.

1471
01:07:34.000 --> 01:07:39.560
Now he has this huge task where he has to go make this very public apology to his coworkers

1472
01:07:39.560 --> 01:07:43.280
and they have to sign that they received his apology.

1473
01:07:43.620 --> 01:07:44.080
Yes.

1474
01:07:44.300 --> 01:07:46.540
That's going to be now Dwight's task.

1475
01:07:47.060 --> 01:07:54.720
Meanwhile, we've got this very interesting, somewhat odd other storyline that's going

1476
01:07:54.720 --> 01:07:55.260
to come up.

1477
01:07:55.400 --> 01:07:57.700
It really seems like it comes out of nowhere.

1478
01:07:57.980 --> 01:07:59.260
It's in the break room.

1479
01:07:59.500 --> 01:08:02.420
Andy, I guess, is really good at pirating movies.

1480
01:08:02.540 --> 01:08:04.520
So you can see them before they come out.

1481
01:08:04.520 --> 01:08:04.880
Mm-hmm.

1482
01:08:05.120 --> 01:08:09.480
And Jim and Pam are going to watch this movie with Andy on his laptop.

1483
01:08:10.280 --> 01:08:10.660
Yes.

1484
01:08:10.940 --> 01:08:13.800
We got a lot of fan mail about this pirated movie scene.

1485
01:08:14.560 --> 01:08:16.820
Hannah E., Abby S., and Bet S.

1486
01:08:17.140 --> 01:08:17.420
said,

1487
01:08:17.820 --> 01:08:22.900
I am absolutely obsessed with the strange mini movie Andy watches with Jack Black and

1488
01:08:22.900 --> 01:08:24.260
several other big names.

1489
01:08:24.260 --> 01:08:26.700
How did this subplot come about?

1490
01:08:27.180 --> 01:08:28.720
Does it rhyme with Schmooper Bowl?

1491
01:08:29.080 --> 01:08:30.020
It does.

1492
01:08:30.300 --> 01:08:31.280
It does.

1493
01:08:31.820 --> 01:08:34.140
Remember when I said there was that extra scrutiny?

1494
01:08:34.720 --> 01:08:39.560
Well, one of the things that the network was very insistent about was that this episode

1495
01:08:39.560 --> 01:08:41.920
have big name guest stars.

1496
01:08:42.200 --> 01:08:43.720
So they could flash it about.

1497
01:08:43.920 --> 01:08:44.340
Yeah.

1498
01:08:44.580 --> 01:08:45.340
Jack Black.

1499
01:08:45.900 --> 01:08:47.040
Jessica Alba.

1500
01:08:47.320 --> 01:08:47.840
Yes.

1501
01:08:48.260 --> 01:08:52.840
There was a lot of comparison to when other shows had run after the Super Bowl, like Friends,

1502
01:08:52.840 --> 01:08:54.880
who had featured big guest stars.

1503
01:08:55.180 --> 01:09:00.300
But Greg and the rest of our writers were very against this.

1504
01:09:01.260 --> 01:09:05.180
Especially against it was Allison Jones, our casting director.

1505
01:09:05.560 --> 01:09:11.500
They all felt that to have like a big name guest star walk into the office pretending to

1506
01:09:11.500 --> 01:09:16.640
play a character at a small paper company would just totally shatter the reality of the

1507
01:09:16.640 --> 01:09:18.400
documentary premise of our show.

1508
01:09:18.640 --> 01:09:21.460
We would get all these new eyes on the episode maybe,

1509
01:09:21.460 --> 01:09:25.180
but the conceit of our show is that it's a documentary.

1510
01:09:25.700 --> 01:09:26.140
That's right.

1511
01:09:26.260 --> 01:09:28.940
You can't have Jack Black come in and pretend to be a salesman.

1512
01:09:29.360 --> 01:09:29.880
Exactly.

1513
01:09:29.880 --> 01:09:33.980
But you can years later have James Spader play Robert California.

1514
01:09:34.180 --> 01:09:35.900
And have Idris Elba come in.

1515
01:09:36.060 --> 01:09:36.110
I know.

1516
01:09:36.110 --> 01:09:37.040
And all these other people.

1517
01:09:37.080 --> 01:09:37.860
And Timothy Oliphant.

1518
01:09:38.260 --> 01:09:40.200
And Kathy Bates.

1519
01:09:41.040 --> 01:09:41.560
Okay.

1520
01:09:41.720 --> 01:09:42.520
But for now.

1521
01:09:42.760 --> 01:09:43.300
For now.

1522
01:09:43.500 --> 01:09:45.060
Our integrity is intact.

1523
01:09:45.860 --> 01:09:52.860
And Greg came up with this idea, this fix, that would not infect the reality of the show.

1524
01:09:53.040 --> 01:09:57.660
And that was where the idea for Pam, Jim, and Andy to watch this pirated movie.

1525
01:09:58.220 --> 01:10:03.180
And I guess Terry Weinberg, who was one of our original executive producers,

1526
01:10:03.180 --> 01:10:07.920
was now working as the executive vice president of NBC Entertainment.

1527
01:10:08.200 --> 01:10:14.000
And Greg said that she was really instrumental in fighting like the kind of top brass at NBC

1528
01:10:14.000 --> 01:10:17.320
to agree to this fix.

1529
01:10:17.960 --> 01:10:18.940
They did.

1530
01:10:19.460 --> 01:10:21.760
Jack Black was the first person to commit.

1531
01:10:22.060 --> 01:10:22.980
He was all in.

1532
01:10:23.060 --> 01:10:24.060
He loved our show.

1533
01:10:24.600 --> 01:10:25.580
Cloris Leachman.

1534
01:10:26.300 --> 01:10:27.600
Amazing, by the way.

1535
01:10:27.800 --> 01:10:28.440
Amazing.

1536
01:10:28.440 --> 01:10:31.920
She heard a pitch on what the story would be.

1537
01:10:32.000 --> 01:10:34.200
And she was like, yes, I am in.

1538
01:10:34.380 --> 01:10:36.920
And then finally, we got Jessica Alba.

1539
01:10:37.380 --> 01:10:41.160
So the movie is called Mrs. Albert Hannity.

1540
01:10:41.800 --> 01:10:43.980
And Jack Black is playing Sam.

1541
01:10:44.180 --> 01:10:46.540
Cloris Leachman is playing Lily, a.k.a.

1542
01:10:46.700 --> 01:10:46.940
Nana.

1543
01:10:47.240 --> 01:10:49.460
And Jessica Alba plays Sophie.

1544
01:10:49.760 --> 01:10:52.800
It's sort of a romantic love triangle story.

1545
01:10:53.120 --> 01:10:58.100
Yeah, Jack Black is dating or engaged to Jessica Alba's character.

1546
01:10:58.100 --> 01:11:01.100
And she's introducing him to her grandmother.

1547
01:11:01.320 --> 01:11:03.340
And there's an instant connection.

1548
01:11:03.640 --> 01:11:06.820
I mean, they go to shake hands and music starts playing.

1549
01:11:07.220 --> 01:11:09.000
Yeah, there's some electricity there.

1550
01:11:09.220 --> 01:11:13.380
Well, I want you to know there were some alt ideas for this parody movie, Jenna.

1551
01:11:13.720 --> 01:11:14.060
Oh.

1552
01:11:14.160 --> 01:11:18.040
And I went back to the table read draft, not the shooting draft,

1553
01:11:18.160 --> 01:11:21.140
just to see what it said in the table read.

1554
01:11:21.340 --> 01:11:25.880
In the table read draft, the movie was going to be called Hang Glider Cop.

1555
01:11:26.460 --> 01:11:26.820
What?

1556
01:11:27.760 --> 01:11:33.140
And Jack Black would be a cop named Tanner that's kind of a rogue cop.

1557
01:11:33.160 --> 01:11:37.600
And he gets, as punishment, sent over to the hang gliding division.

1558
01:11:38.180 --> 01:11:38.660
Okay.

1559
01:11:38.800 --> 01:11:40.800
And now he's going to be a hang gliding cop.

1560
01:11:40.940 --> 01:11:42.120
A wacky comedy.

1561
01:11:42.280 --> 01:11:43.920
Like a cop comedy.

1562
01:11:44.240 --> 01:11:44.520
Okay.

1563
01:11:44.860 --> 01:11:46.100
They didn't go with that one.

1564
01:11:47.060 --> 01:11:50.100
Probably getting a hang glider was too much of her project.

1565
01:11:50.540 --> 01:11:52.160
Gosh, I'd love to see that movie.

1566
01:11:52.360 --> 01:11:53.520
Hang Glider Cop.

1567
01:11:53.520 --> 01:11:55.260
Jack Black, are you listening?

1568
01:11:55.480 --> 01:11:55.800
Mm-hmm.

1569
01:11:56.200 --> 01:11:57.040
HG division.

1570
01:11:57.540 --> 01:11:59.920
We got more fan questions about this.

1571
01:12:00.220 --> 01:12:03.780
Livian G, Norit F, and Maddie L said,

1572
01:12:03.940 --> 01:12:07.460
did we get to meet Jack Black, Cloris Leachman, or Jessica Alba?

1573
01:12:08.560 --> 01:12:09.100
No.

1574
01:12:09.500 --> 01:12:11.600
We did not work the same day as they worked.

1575
01:12:11.600 --> 01:12:18.200
They filmed all of their stuff in one day at a private residence in West L.A.

1576
01:12:18.400 --> 01:12:20.560
The rest of us all had the day off.

1577
01:12:20.740 --> 01:12:23.160
They didn't even come to our base camp.

1578
01:12:23.320 --> 01:12:24.680
No, they were at a house.

1579
01:12:24.880 --> 01:12:26.640
I looked it up on the call sheet.

1580
01:12:26.780 --> 01:12:28.520
They started really early that day.

1581
01:12:28.880 --> 01:12:34.920
On the call sheet, it said breakfast would be ready for the crew at 442 a.m.

1582
01:12:35.100 --> 01:12:36.160
in a nearby park.

1583
01:12:36.160 --> 01:12:36.760
Oof.

1584
01:12:36.960 --> 01:12:39.000
They had to get everything in one day.

1585
01:12:39.280 --> 01:12:39.540
Yeah.

1586
01:12:39.760 --> 01:12:41.700
The actors all arrived really early.

1587
01:12:41.980 --> 01:12:46.220
They did their hair, makeup, and wardrobe fittings all in the morning.

1588
01:12:46.600 --> 01:12:52.780
And then they were finally allowed to go into the neighborhood where the house was located at 7 a.m.

1589
01:12:52.880 --> 01:12:57.800
So they had vans that took everyone from this park base camp over to the location.

1590
01:12:58.260 --> 01:13:00.520
And that's where they filmed it.

1591
01:13:00.800 --> 01:13:01.980
So we never met.

1592
01:13:01.980 --> 01:13:08.060
So while they're watching Mrs. Albert Hannity, we start seeing Pam getting all these text messages.

1593
01:13:08.360 --> 01:13:13.660
And we learn this storyline that Pam's parents are in a rough patch.

1594
01:13:14.280 --> 01:13:18.100
Yes, and that Pam's dad is bunking with Jim and Pam.

1595
01:13:18.600 --> 01:13:23.760
It is really funny, though, that Jim and Pam are having these little sidebar relationship conversations.

1596
01:13:23.760 --> 01:13:25.680
And Andy thinks it's about the movie.

1597
01:13:25.940 --> 01:13:28.680
Andy thinks you guys are just like geniuses at relationships.

1598
01:13:28.760 --> 01:13:30.900
That you can just figure all this stuff out.

1599
01:13:30.900 --> 01:13:35.980
Well, something else I should mention, Angela, is that we were actually watching this movie.

1600
01:13:35.980 --> 01:13:37.660
That's one of my questions for you.

1601
01:13:37.740 --> 01:13:42.200
I was like, ask Jenna, were they actually watching the movie on the laptop?

1602
01:13:42.560 --> 01:13:43.520
So we were.

1603
01:13:43.740 --> 01:13:46.640
How could you not react to Cloris coming out of the tub?

1604
01:13:46.800 --> 01:13:48.620
You had to be distracted on your phone.

1605
01:13:48.760 --> 01:13:50.120
I was like, holy crap.

1606
01:13:50.860 --> 01:13:53.500
So they had shot this a long time ago.

1607
01:13:53.500 --> 01:14:01.740
If you look at the call sheets for this episode, this bit of us in the conference room was not even on the schedule for these nine days.

1608
01:14:02.040 --> 01:14:11.000
We shot this another week later so that they could put together this mini movie so that we could have some reactions.

1609
01:14:11.520 --> 01:14:15.720
The first time they played them for us, we couldn't speak.

1610
01:14:15.840 --> 01:14:16.980
We were riveted.

1611
01:14:17.220 --> 01:14:18.800
We were like, what are we watching?

1612
01:14:18.820 --> 01:14:20.020
That was what I thought.

1613
01:14:20.140 --> 01:14:24.940
I was like, how can Jim and Pam not just be falling out of their chairs right now?

1614
01:14:25.040 --> 01:14:28.000
And Andy's like, guys, they're making out.

1615
01:14:29.540 --> 01:14:39.960
So what they did was they showed it to us, and then we watched a blank screen, but we knew what we were supposed to be reacting to.

1616
01:14:40.020 --> 01:14:41.100
You knew the beats of it.

1617
01:14:41.160 --> 01:14:41.520
Yes.

1618
01:14:41.680 --> 01:14:41.840
Yeah.

1619
01:14:41.960 --> 01:14:45.100
And then they inserted it into the screen.

1620
01:14:45.300 --> 01:14:47.480
You know, if you notice, it's all over the shoulder.

1621
01:14:47.620 --> 01:14:48.260
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1622
01:14:48.300 --> 01:14:48.660
Onto the thing.

1623
01:14:48.660 --> 01:14:50.140
I was very curious about that.

1624
01:14:50.300 --> 01:14:51.620
Yeah, it was bonkers.

1625
01:14:52.240 --> 01:14:57.180
Well, after all the texting with Pam's mom and dad, Pam says, Jim, can you talk to my dad?

1626
01:14:57.180 --> 01:14:59.260
God, you're so good at talking to people.

1627
01:14:59.260 --> 01:15:00.540
Yeah, maybe he'll open up to you.

1628
01:15:00.680 --> 01:15:00.940
Yeah.

1629
01:15:01.280 --> 01:15:03.880
This is not going to go the way Pam planned.

1630
01:15:04.100 --> 01:15:04.380
Yeah.

1631
01:15:04.760 --> 01:15:06.120
But that's for next week.

1632
01:15:06.460 --> 01:15:11.740
Well, before we close out this episode, Michael has decided to do yoga in the conference room.

1633
01:15:11.980 --> 01:15:12.960
For relaxation.

1634
01:15:13.640 --> 01:15:17.240
It did really make me laugh when he was like, um, if you have your legs open, close them.

1635
01:15:17.340 --> 01:15:22.000
No one needs to see that, um, or whatever he said cracked me up.

1636
01:15:22.020 --> 01:15:26.900
It also really made me laugh when Jim says to Pam, don't open your eyes.

1637
01:15:27.180 --> 01:15:28.400
And she says, why?

1638
01:15:28.540 --> 01:15:29.260
Oh, God.

1639
01:15:29.820 --> 01:15:32.680
I don't know if you noticed Dwight and Angela are laying side by side.

1640
01:15:33.000 --> 01:15:33.420
Oh.

1641
01:15:33.780 --> 01:15:38.180
Yeah, that's because there was a deleted scene where Dwight whispers to her,

1642
01:15:38.380 --> 01:15:43.720
I will make love to you the way I used to if you will sign my apology letter.

1643
01:15:43.760 --> 01:15:45.340
And she's like, ah, no.

1644
01:15:46.700 --> 01:15:47.140
Wow.

1645
01:15:47.540 --> 01:15:52.400
Well, during all of this, Stanley has a little heart monitor on and it beeps whenever he gets stressed.

1646
01:15:52.400 --> 01:15:56.140
Turns out every time Michael gets close to him, it starts beeping.

1647
01:15:56.400 --> 01:15:58.260
And then when Michael walks away, it stops.

1648
01:15:58.600 --> 01:16:01.820
So Michael has this very funny talking head where he says,

1649
01:16:02.000 --> 01:16:05.200
it turns out that Dwight wasn't the killer after all.

1650
01:16:05.340 --> 01:16:06.420
The killer was Michael.

1651
01:16:06.880 --> 01:16:10.200
And he says, quote, you never suspect you're the killer.

1652
01:16:10.780 --> 01:16:11.860
It's a great twiSt.

1653
01:16:12.100 --> 01:16:13.000
Great twiSt.

1654
01:16:13.440 --> 01:16:17.860
My gosh, you guys, that was stress relief part one.

1655
01:16:18.100 --> 01:16:18.640
I know.

1656
01:16:18.640 --> 01:16:19.580
We did it.

1657
01:16:19.700 --> 01:16:21.320
Next week is part two.

1658
01:16:21.540 --> 01:16:21.980
Boom.

1659
01:16:22.200 --> 01:16:22.660
Roasted.

1660
